    "title": "Portadown News, 18 June 1949, p. 6 (\"Unionists' Great Triumph: Election in Lurgan\"); nominations in the Lurgan Mail, 4 June 1949, p. 5, and the Portadown News, 11 June 1949, p. 3",
    "publisher": "Portadown News (via the British Newspaper Archive)",
    "kind": "news",
    "check": "every figure read from the page image"
  },
  "note": "First election of Lurgan Borough Council, polled Wednesday 15 June 1949. The Governor approved a charter of incorporation giving the urban district borough status in May 1949 (Belfast Telegraph, 18 May 1949, p. 7; Lurgan Mail, 21 May 1949, p. 5): three aldermen and twelve councillors, all elected by the whole borough; nomination day 1 June. The borough came into being on Thursday 7 July 1949 (Lurgan Mail, 3 September 1949, p. 3). Four candidates stood for the three aldermanships and seventeen for the twelve councillorships; \"all fifteen candidates nominated officially were returned with resounding majorities over their Labour and Independent opponents\"; over 85 per cent of the 6,200 electors voted. Labels as printed: U Unionist, L Labour, I Independent. Two candidates named David Patterson stood: the Unionist (of Lake Street, as printed) was elected and the Independent polled 503."
}
